  ],
  "equipment_type": "Commercial boiler controller",
  "applies_to": "RBI (Mestek) Futera III, Fusion and CK Series boilers with a HeatNet V3 control board, including HeatNet cascades of up to 16 boilers.",
  "summary": "The HeatNet V3 control on RBI FIII, Fusion and CK boilers exposes a fixed BACnet object list. The BMS writes heat demand, the system setpoint (guarded by a countdown failsafe timer), outdoor-reset settings, DHW setpoint, clock and flow/boiler limits as analog and binary values. Read-only analog inputs give plant temperatures, counts and per-boiler run time, cycles, temperatures and modulation, and read-only binary values give interlock, alarm and status flags for each of up to 16 boilers.",
  "bacnet_transport": [],
  "firmware": "HeatNet V3; BTUH, system return/flow and boiler-count points need firmware 2.00 or later",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The object list does not say which BACnet data link (BACnet IP or BACnet MS/TP) is used and gives no device instance or network settings.",
    "Per-boiler binary values are printed once as Boiler##_<name> with an instance formula; they are listed here at the boiler 1 instance. Boiler n = 1000-series base + (n - 1) x 32, or 2000/3000-series base + (n - 1) x 16. Boiler 1 is the master or stand-alone (BACnet-connected) boiler; members are 2-16.",
    "Per-boiler analog inputs are printed as ranges and listed here for boiler 1 only: Boiler01-16_Runtime AI 48-63, _Cycles AI 64-79, _SupplyTemp AI 80-95, _ReturnTemp AI 96-111, _DHWTemp AI 112-127, _Modulation AI 128-143 (boiler n = boiler 1 instance + n - 1).",
    "No objects are printed at BV 1014, BV 1022 or BV 3004-3008.",
    "The manual describes Boiler##_OutsideSensorNA as 'Header Sensor not available', the same text as HeaderSensorNA; the name suggests the outside sensor.",
    "Temperatures are in °F."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "RBI FIII/Fusion/CK Series Boiler - HeatNet V3 BACnet Objects",
    "doc_number": "V1.00",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.literature.mestek.com/dms/RBI%20Water%20Heaters/RBI%20V3%20BACnet%20Objects%20v1.00.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "Connect the BMS to the master (boiler 1) HeatNet board. Write BV 1 HeatDemand to call for heat and AV 2 Setpoint for the system setpoint, and keep reloading AV 1 SetpointTimer so the plant does not fall back to its local setpoint. Read header/supply/return temperatures, boilers on, modulation and the per-boiler alarm and failed flags.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 1",
        "name": "HeatDemand",
        "why": "Heat demand from the BMS (1 = heat)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 2",
        "name": "Setpoint",
        "why": "System setpoint, 40-220 °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 1",
        "name": "SetpointTimer",
        "why": "Failsafe countdown; reload before it reaches 0"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 144",
        "name": "OperatingSetpoint",
        "why": "Active setpoint in use"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 3",
        "name": "HeaderTemp",
        "why": "Header / system temperature, °F"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "BoilersOn",
        "why": "Number of boilers running"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 2",
        "name": "Modulation",
        "why": "System target modulation, %"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1005",
        "name": "Boiler##_Running",
        "why": "Boiler 1 firing (add 32 per boiler number)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1002",
        "name": "Boiler##_Alarm",
        "why": "Boiler 1 alarm (add 32 per boiler number)"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 1003",
        "name": "Boiler##_Failed",
        "why": "Boiler 1 failed (add 32 per boiler number)"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BV 1 HeatDemand puts the boiler (plant) into heating mode when set to 1; 0 removes the demand. The setpoint the BMS writes is AV 2 Setpoint.",
    "heartbeat": "AV 1 SetpointTimer (0-65535 s) is a BMS failsafe countdown. The BMS must reload it periodically; if it reaches zero the control assumes the BMS has stopped and reloads its own saved local setpoint. Writing any read/write variable reloads the timer to 60 s if it is below 60 (on firmware below 3.48 only writing the setpoint does this).",
    "remote_sensors": "AV 16 BMSFlowRateGPM lets the BMS supply the system flow for flow-limited control, and AV 17 BMSLimitBoilers caps how many boilers HeatNet may run. AV 3-7 and BV 2 set up outdoor air reset; there is no writable outdoor temperature.",
    "setup": [
      "The object document gives no data link, address or device-instance settings.",
      "To set the clock, write AV 8-14 (month, day, year, hour, minute, second, weekday) and then write 1 to BV 3 SetClock."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "If SetpointTimer runs out, the plant quietly returns to its local setpoint.",
      "Per-boiler objects are listed at the boiler 1 instance; offset them by boiler number using the formulas in the notes. Boiler 1 is the master or stand-alone boiler.",
      "Modulation per boiler (AI 128-143) does not work in AA/High Fire, T1 or T2 modes.",
      "Several points need firmware 2.00 or later."
    ]
  },
